  "metadata": {
    "title": "Goldilocks CGCNN crystal representation",
    "description": "<p>A crystal graph convolutional neural network published for the learned representation it produces, not for the class it predicts. Goldilocks embeds its pooled 64-dimensional crystal representation, taken before the classification head, as one block of the k-distance model's input vector.</p><p>The network was trained against Materials Project <code>is_metal</code> labels from an autumn 2025 snapshot after removal of structural duplicates. Class 0 denotes insulator and class 1 denotes metal.</p><p><strong>It is not published as a usable metallicity classifier.</strong> It carries no decision threshold, and the surviving record describes no held-out split against which one could be chosen, so nothing here says at what score a structure should be called metallic or how often the answer would be right. <code>model.json</code> records its role as <code>feature_extractor</code>, and Goldilocks software declines to serve it as a model. For metallicity prediction with a stated threshold and measured accuracy, use the Goldilocks CGCNN metallicity classifier trained on Matbench <code>mp_is_metal</code>.</p><p>The record contains the checkpoint, its atomic embedding table, and <code>model.json</code> describing the graph construction, the architecture, and the digests of both files. That record was written after the fact rather than by the run that fitted the network, and says so.</p>",
